Question: I am using typeorm and postgres database. I want to store a json object in my entity.
<code>import { Entity, Column, PrimaryGeneratedColumn } from "typeorm";

@Entity()
export class User {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
  id: number;

  @Column()
  name: string;

  @Column()
  json: string;
}
</code>
I am using <code>string</code> type for <code>json</code> column. But I am not sure if this is the best way to do it.
Is there any other type I can use?
Answer: You can use <code>Json</code> type.
<code>import { Entity, Column, PrimaryGeneratedColumn } from "typeorm";

@Entity()
export class User {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
  id: number;

  @Column()
  name: string;

  @Column({ type: 'json' })
  json: any;
}
</code>
Answer: You can use <code>Json</code> type.
